# Environment of the delivery agent, read by deploy/mes-courses-agent.service.
# Copy to /etc/mes-courses/agent.env, fill in the values, then:
#   chown root:root /etc/mes-courses/agent.env && chmod 600 /etc/mes-courses/agent.env
# Never commit the filled-in file.

# The repository whose channel releases the agent reads, owner/name.
GITHUB_REPOSITORY=
# A fine-grained personal access token, read-only (Contents: read) on that one repository.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# DSN of the Sentry project mes-courses-server (EU region). Empty: reports go to the journal,
# and the agent sends no check-in.
#
# Alert, to configure once in Sentry (the agent cannot): in the project mes-courses-server, add an
# issue alert rule that
#   - applies in every environment (staging and production),
#   - fires on new issues, and on monitor issues (the monitor `mes-courses-agent` missing or
#     failing a check-in: a stopped agent, a degraded instance, a Pi that is down),
#   - filters on the tag component equals delivery-agent,
#   - emails the maintainer.
# Without it, a failed staging deployment is visible in Sentry but not emailed (FR-020, FR-020a).
SENTRY_DSN=
